{
	"_note": "Hachiro the smith and handyman: lives in the Kurogane Smithy (the north-east house): off hours he is at the anvil behind the counter (out of sight, the smithy's door is shut then) and in bed (away) from 21:00. On work days he mends the roof of Kota's family house south of the road early, keeps the smithy counter (the smithy map's keeper spot) 10:00-16:00, so talking to him there opens the shop (data/shops.json keeper), and looks at the pond in the evening. In bad weather he only works the forge; Sundays he fishes (the smithy is shut); on his birthday the smithy stays shut too: the shrine in the morning, the pond until 16:00. While a house extension is under way (the house_work flag, Game.sync_build_flag; any weather but a storm, Sundays too, since the job has a day it is due; a day he does not build is not counted, data/shops.json builds plan) he builds on the farm: out the village's west road at 7:30, hammering at the farmhouse's front wall west of the door from about 8:20, fetching boards from the lumber stack left of the house front now and then, lunch standing by the wall at 12:00, back to the smithy for the evening at 17:00; the smithy counter has nobody then (data/shops.json builds away). Gifts: rice balls, eels, catfish and good ore (hoshigane best); a plain grey stone is an insult. Of the kitchen's dishes, hearty ones (grilled fish, fish and daikon, potato stew best); no sweets. Format: README.md, Villagers.",
